{"title":"SSC MTS 2020 Biology PART-4","slug":"ssc-mts-2020-biology-part-4","questions":[{"question":"Which bacterium is responsible for peptic ulcers?","option_1":"Bacillius cereus","option_2":"Helicobacter pylori","option_3":"Escherichia coli","option_4":"Campylobacter","answer":"2","solution":""},{"question":"Complex food substances break down into simpler ones with the help of:","option_1":"bacteria","option_2":"hormones","option_3":"fungi","option_4":"enzymes","answer":"4","solution":""},{"question":"______ contains an enzyme called lingual lipase, which breaks down fats.","option_1":"The small intestine","option_2":"The stomach","option_3":"Saliva","option_4":"The large intestine","answer":"3","solution":""},{"question":"Which goats' underfur is woven into fine shawls called Pashmina shawls?","option_1":"Alpine goat","option_2":"Boer goat","option_3":"Kashmiri goat","option_4":"Jamnapari goat","answer":"3","solution":""},{"question":"What is the network of air tubes for gas exchange in insects?","option_1":"Diaphragm","option_2":"Tracheae","option_3":"Spiracles","option_4":"Gills","answer":"2","solution":""},{"question":"Energy and carbon requirements of the autotrophic organism are fulfilled by ______.","option_1":"lysis","option_2":"prognosis","option_3":"photosynthesis","option_4":"glycolysis","answer":"3","solution":""},{"question":"Which part of the digestive system receives secretions from the liver and the pancreas?","option_1":"Large intestines","option_2":"Stomach","option_3":"Small intestines","option_4":"Gall bladder","answer":"3","solution":""},{"question":"Plants release water into the air by the process of ______.","option_1":"tropism","option_2":"photoperiodism","option_3":"transpiration","option_4":"photosynthesis","answer":"3","solution":""},{"question":"The human shoulder joint is an example of a ______ joint.","option_1":"fixed","option_2":"ball and socket","option_3":"hinge","option_4":"pivotal","answer":"2","solution":""},{"question":"‘Myopia’ is also known as:","option_1":"far-sightedness","option_2":"near-sightedness","option_3":"astigmatism","option_4":"presbyopia","answer":"2","solution":""},{"question":"Which of the following causative agents causes the disease Ebola?","option_1":"Protozoan","option_2":"Bacteria","option_3":"Fungus","option_4":"Virus","answer":"4","solution":""},{"question":"Which of the following diseases is caused by fungus?","option_1":"Small pox","option_2":"Ringworm","option_3":"Diarrhoea","option_4":"Polio","answer":"2","solution":""},{"question":"What is the full form of OCD?","option_1":"Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder","option_2":"Obesity-Controlling Device","option_3":"Obesity-Compulsive Disorder","option_4":"Obsession-Controlling Device","answer":"1","solution":""},{"question":"A/an ______ is any substance that causes your immune system to produce antibodies against it.","option_1":"antigen","option_2":"protein","option_3":"platelet","option_4":"glucose","answer":"1","solution":""}]}